      "name" : "Baklava",
      "ingredients" : "\t•\t1 package (16 oz) phyllo dough, thawed\n\t•\t2 cups walnuts or pistachios, finely chopped\n\t•\t1 teaspoon cinnamon\n\t•\t1 cup (2 sticks) unsalted butter, melted\n\t•\t1 cup honey\n\t•\t½ cup sugar\n\t•\t½ cup water\n\t•\t1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n\t•\t1 teaspoon lemon juice",
      "hasBeenOpened" : false,
      "steps" : "1. Preheat oven to 175°C. Grease a 9x13-inch baking dish.\n2. Mix nuts & cinnamon in a bowl.\n3. Layer phyllo dough: Place one sheet in the dish, brush with butter, and repeat for about 8 layers.\n4. Add nuts: Sprinkle a layer of nut mixture.\n5. Repeat layering: Add 4 more layers of phyllo (buttered), then more nuts. Repeat until all ingredients are used, finishing with about 8 layers of phyllo.\n6. Cut into diamond shapes before baking.\n7. Bake for 45 minutes until golden brown.\n8. Make syrup: In a saucepan, heat honey, sugar, water, lemon juice, and vanilla. Simmer for 5 minutes.\n9. Pour syrup over hot baklava. Let it soak and cool before serving.\n\nEnjoy your homemade baklava! 🥮✨\n",
      "unlockDate" : 759884400
    },
    {
      "ingredients" : "• 1 whole duck (about 4-5 lbs) 🦆  \n• 1 tablespoon salt 🧂  \n• 1 tablespoon five-spice powder. 🧂  \n• 2 tablespoons honey 🍯  \n• 2 tablespoons soy sauce 🥢  \n• 1 tablespoon rice vinegar 🍚  \n• 1 cup boiling water 💧  \n\nFor serving:  \n• Mandarin pancakes or thin flour tortillas 🥞  \n• Hoisin sauce 🍶  \n• Sliced cucumber and green onions 🥒🧅  \n",
      "name" : "Peking Duck Recipe",
      "unlockDate" : 759970800,
