ie9RFuplUAAOf51ySPWXwGfKBg1BieV\/EFQsFpjj5nNAHs\/wCxpI6fF222EjKjP500J7H9IHh3nTjnnC\/0qyCCb\/WmgCVOtAGmveswJFoMx1avczP\/2Q==",
      "steps" : "1. Prepare the duck: Rinse and pat dry. Rub with salt and five-spice powder inside and out.\n\n2. Glaze the duck: Mix honey, soy sauce, and vinegar. Brush the duck with this mixture.\n\n3. Air-dry: Hang or place the duck on a rack in the fridge, uncovered, for at least 2 hours (or overnight) to dry the skin.\n\n4. Roast: Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C). Place the duck on a rack in a roasting pan. Pour 1 cup of boiling water into the pan (to keep the meat moist).\n\n5. Bake: Roast for about 1 hour 30 minutes, basting with the glaze every 30 minutes. The skin should turn crispy and golden.\n\n6. Rest & Serve: Let it rest for 10 minutes, then slice thinly. Serve with pancakes, hoisin sauce, and veggies.\n\nEnjoy your homemade Peking Duck! 🦆✨"
    },
    {
      "ingredients" : "For the Dough:\n\t•\t250 g all-purpose flour\n\t•\t1\/4 teaspoon salt\n\t•\t1 large egg\n\t•\t80 ml lukewarm water\n\t•\t30 ml vegetable oil or melted butter\n\nFor the Filling:\n\t•\t4-5 medium apples (around 700 g, peeled, cored, and thinly sliced)\n\t•\t70 g granulated sugar\n\t•\t50 g raisins (optional, soaked in 30 ml warm water or rum for 15 minutes)\n\t•\t50 g breadcrumbs\n\t•\t30 g chopped walnuts or almonds (optional)\n\t•\t1 teaspoon ground cinnamon\n\t•\t1\/4 teaspoon ground nutmeg\n\t•\tZest of 1 lemon\n\t•\t30 ml butter (for toasting breadcrumbs)\n\nFor Assembly:\n\t•\t45 ml melted butter (for brushing dough)\n\t•\tPowdered sugar (for garnish)\n",
      "name" : "Apfelstrudel (Apple Strudel)",
      "steps" : "1. Prepare the Dough:\n- In a mixing bowl, combine the flour and salt. Make a well in the center and add the egg, water, and oil.\n- Mix until a dough forms, then knead on a lightly floured surface for about 8-10 minutes until smooth and elastic.\n- Shape the dough into a ball, brush it with oil, cover it with plastic wrap, and let it rest for at least 30 minutes.\n\n2. Prepare the Filling:\n- In a skillet, melt the butter over medium heat. Add the breadcrumbs and toast until golden brown. Set aside to cool.\n- In a large bowl, combine the sliced apples, sugar, soaked and drained raisins, nuts (if using), cinnamon, nutmeg, and lemon zest.\n\n3. Roll Out the Dough:\n- Preheat the oven to 190°C and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.\n- On a clean, lightly floured surface (or a large clean cloth), roll the dough into a thin rectangle. Then, using your hands, carefully stretch it as thin as possible without tearing it—ideally, you should be able to see through it.\n\n4. Assemble the Strudel:\n- Brush the entire surface of the stretched dough with melted butter.\n- Sprinkle the toasted breadcrumbs evenly over the dough, leaving about 5 cm of space along the edges.\n- Spread the apple filling evenly over the breadcrumbs.\n- Fold the short edges of the dough inward, then carefully roll the strudel into a log, starting from one of the long sides. Use the cloth or your hands to help roll it tightly but gently.\n\n5. Bake the Strudel:\n- Place the strudel seam-side down on the prepared baking sheet. Brush the top with melted butter.\n- Bake in the preheated oven for 35-45 minutes, or until golden brown and crisp, brushing with more melted butter halfway through baking.\n\n6. Serve:\n- Allow the strudel to cool slightly, then dust it with powdered sugar.\n- Slice and serve warm, optionally with whipped cream, vanilla ice cream, or vanilla sauce.\n\nEnjoy your delicious homemade Apfelstrudel! 🍏🥧",
      "unlockDate" : 760057200,
