    },
    {
      "steps" : "1. Prepare the Sausages:\n- Heat a skillet or grill over medium heat and add a small amount of vegetable oil.\n- Cook the bratwurst sausages until golden brown and fully cooked, turning occasionally. This usually takes about 8-10 minutes.\n- Remove the sausages from the skillet and let them rest. Slice them into bite-sized pieces before serving.\n\n2. Make the Curry Sauce:\n- In a medium saucepan, heat the vegetable oil over medium heat. Add the chopped onion and sauté until soft and translucent, about 3-4 minutes.\n- Stir in the curry powder, paprika, and cayenne pepper (if using), and cook for 30 seconds to release the spices’ aroma.\n- Add the tomato ketchup, Worcestershire sauce, sugar, vinegar, and water. Mix well.\n- Bring the sauce to a gentle simmer and cook for 5-7 minutes, stirring occasionally. Adjust the consistency with more water if needed.\n- Taste and season with salt, pepper, or additional spices as desired.\n\n3. Assemble and Serve:\n- Arrange the sliced sausages on a plate or shallow bowl.\n- Generously pour the curry sauce over the sausages.\n- Sprinkle extra curry powder on top for garnish and serve with crusty bread, French fries, or potato wedges.\n\nEnjoy your delicious Currywurst, a true German classic! 🌭🇩🇪",
